{"question_text": {"(Pathology) Tuberculosis, Pneumonia, Bronchial Carcinoma, Chronic Bronchitis, Empyema, Bronchiectasis, Respiratory failure, Pleurisy, Pleural effusions, Pneumoconiosis": [{"id": "1", "question": "১) What is the neoplasm of pleura?", "option1": "mesothelioma", "option2": "myxoma", "option3": "hamartoma", "option4": "pleuroma", "answer": "1", "exp": "<div class=\"qMYqUG_convSearchResultHighlightRoot\">\r\n<div class=\"\" data-turn-id-container=\"request-6a83414b-92f8-83e9-901e-ae9b28767c93-67\" data-is-intersecting=\"true\">\r\n<section class=\"text-token-text-primary w-full focus:outline-none has-data-writing-block:pointer-events-none [&amp;:has([data-writing-block])&gt;*]:pointer-events-auto R6Vx5W_threadScrollVars scroll-mb-[calc(var(--scroll-root-safe-area-inset-bottom,0px)+var(--thread-response-height))] scroll-mt-[calc(var(--header-height)+min(200px,max(70px,20svh)))]\" dir=\"auto\" data-turn-id=\"request-6a83414b-92f8-83e9-901e-ae9b28767c93-67\" data-turn-id-container=\"request-6a83414b-92f8-83e9-901e-ae9b28767c93-67\" data-testid=\"conversation-turn-918\" data-turn=\"assistant\">\r\n<div class=\"text-base my-auto mx-auto pb-8 [--thread-content-margin:var(--thread-content-margin-xs,calc(var(--spacing)*4))] @w-sm/main:[--thread-content-margin:var(--thread-content-margin-sm,calc(var(--spacing)*6))] @w-lg/main:[--thread-content-margin:var(--thread-content-margin-lg,calc(var(--spacing)*16))] px-(--thread-content-margin)\">\r\n<div data-conversation-screenshot-content=\"\" class=\"[--thread-content-max-width:40rem] @w-lg/main:[--thread-content-max-width:48rem] mx-auto max-w-(--thread-content-max-width) flex-1 group/turn-messages focus-visible:outline-hidden relative flex w-full min-w-0 flex-col agent-turn\">\r\n<div class=\"flex max-w-full flex-col gap-4 grow\">\r\n<div data-message-author-role=\"assistant\" data-message-id=\"7a1ff051-9a95-4d81-b0d4-001704321366\" dir=\"auto\" data-message-model-slug=\"gpt-5-6-mini\" class=\"min-h-8 text-message relative flex w-full flex-col items-end gap-2 text-start break-words whitespace-normal outline-none keyboard-focused:focus-ring [.text-message+&amp;]:mt-1\" data-turn-start-message=\"true\" tabindex=\"0\">\r\n<div class=\"flex w-full flex-col gap-1 empty:hidden\">\r\n<div class=\"fbskMG_root yWcLfW_streamingContainer markdown prose dark:prose-invert wrap-break-word w-full dark markdown-new-styling\">\r\n<p data-start=\"51\" data-end=\"219\" class=\"PDq2pG_selectionAnchorContainer\"><strong data-start=\"70\" data-end=\"86\">Mesothelioma</strong><span> </span>is a malignant neoplasm arising from the<span> </span><strong data-start=\"128\" data-end=\"164\">mesothelial lining of the pleura</strong>. It is strongly associated with<span> </span><strong data-start=\"197\" data-end=\"218\">asbestos exposure</strong>.</p>\r\n<ul data-start=\"221\" data-end=\"379\">\r\n<li data-start=\"221\" data-end=\"248\">\r\n<p data-start=\"223\" data-end=\"248\"><strong data-start=\"223\" data-end=\"248\">Mesothelioma → pleura</strong></p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"249\" data-end=\"278\">\r\n<p data-start=\"251\" data-end=\"278\"><strong data-start=\"251\" data-end=\"278\">Myxoma → commonly heart</strong></p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"279\" data-end=\"319\">\r\n<p data-start=\"281\" data-end=\"319\"><strong data-start=\"281\" data-end=\"319\">Hamartoma → commonly lung (benign)</strong></p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"320\" data-end=\"379\">\r\n<p data-start=\"322\" data-end=\"379\"><strong data-start=\"322\" data-end=\"379\">Pleuroma → not a standard recognized pleural neoplasm</strong></p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p data-start=\"381\" data-end=\"449\" data-is-last-node=\"\" data-is-only-node=\"\"><strong data-start=\"381\" data-end=\"396\">Exam pearl:</strong><br data-start=\"396\" data-end=\"399\"><strong data-start=\"399\" data-end=\"449\" data-is-last-node=\"\">“Malignant neoplasm of pleura = Mesothelioma.”</strong></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"z-0 flex min-h-[46px] justify-start\"></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div data-conversation-screenshot-content=\"\" class=\"[--thread-content-max-width:40rem] @w-lg/main:[--thread-content-max-width:48rem] mx-auto max-w-(--thread-content-max-width) flex-1\">\r\n<div></div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</section>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>"}, {"id": "2", "question": "২) Pneumonia is the infection of lung.......?", "option1": "covering", "option2": "parenchyma", "option3": "supporting tissues", "option4": "vasculature", "answer": "2", "exp": "<p data-start=\"49\" data-end=\"201\"><strong data-start=\"68\" data-end=\"81\">Pneumonia</strong><span> </span>is an<span> </span><strong data-start=\"88\" data-end=\"124\">infection of the lung parenchyma</strong>, particularly involving the<span> </span><strong data-start=\"153\" data-end=\"200\">alveoli and surrounding interstitial tissue</strong>.</p>\r\n<ul data-start=\"203\" data-end=\"351\">\r\n<li data-start=\"203\" data-end=\"244\">\r\n<p data-start=\"205\" data-end=\"244\"><strong data-start=\"205\" data-end=\"244\">Lung parenchyma → site of pneumonia</strong></p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"245\" data-end=\"297\">\r\n<p data-start=\"247\" data-end=\"297\"><strong data-start=\"247\" data-end=\"297\">Pleura (covering) → infection causes pleuritis</strong></p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"298\" data-end=\"351\">\r\n<p data-start=\"300\" data-end=\"351\"><strong data-start=\"300\" data-end=\"351\">Vasculature → infection is not termed pneumonia</strong></p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p data-start=\"353\" data-end=\"418\" data-is-last-node=\"\" data-is-only-node=\"\"><strong data-start=\"353\" data-end=\"368\">Exam pearl:</strong><br data-start=\"368\" data-end=\"371\"><strong data-start=\"371\" data-end=\"418\" data-is-last-node=\"\">“Pneumonia = Infection of lung parenchyma.”</strong></p>"}, {"id": "3", "question": "৩) Which is a criteria of secondary tuberculosis?", "option1": "occurs mainly in children", "option2": "only exogenous source of infection", "option3": "usually sub apical lesion", "option4": "hilar lymph node involved", "answer": "3", "exp": "<p data-start=\"63\" data-end=\"228\"><strong data-start=\"82\" data-end=\"123\">Secondary (post-primary) tuberculosis</strong><span> </span>typically affects the<span> </span><strong data-start=\"146\" data-end=\"197\">apical or posterior segments of the upper lobes</strong>, where oxygen tension is high.</p>\r\n<ul data-start=\"230\" data-end=\"457\">\r\n<li data-start=\"230\" data-end=\"275\">\r\n<p data-start=\"232\" data-end=\"275\"><strong data-start=\"232\" data-end=\"275\">Secondary TB → usually subapical lesion</strong></p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"276\" data-end=\"315\">\r\n<p data-start=\"278\" data-end=\"315\"><strong data-start=\"278\" data-end=\"315\">Primary TB → commonly in children</strong></p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"316\" data-end=\"373\">\r\n<p data-start=\"318\" data-end=\"373\"><strong data-start=\"318\" data-end=\"373\">Primary TB → hilar lymph node involvement is common</strong></p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"374\" data-end=\"457\">\r\n<p data-start=\"376\" data-end=\"457\">Secondary TB may result from<span> </span><strong data-start=\"405\" data-end=\"421\">reactivation</strong><span> </span>of latent infection or reinfection.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p data-start=\"459\" data-end=\"545\" data-is-last-node=\"\" data-is-only-node=\"\" class=\"yWcLfW_streamingTextBlock\"><strong data-start=\"459\" data-end=\"474\">Exam pearl:</strong><br data-start=\"474\" data-end=\"477\"><strong data-start=\"477\" data-end=\"545\" data-is-last-node=\"\">“Secondary TB → upper lobe, especially apical/subapical lesion.”</strong></p>"}, {"id": "4", "question": "৪) Which is the commonest organism for CAP?", "option1": "S. pneumoniae", "option2": "L. pneumoniae", "option3": "K. pneumoniae", "option4": "N. pneumoniae", "answer": "1", "exp": "<div class=\"qMYqUG_convSearchResultHighlightRoot\">\r\n<div class=\"\" data-turn-id-container=\"request-6a83414b-92f8-83e9-901e-ae9b28767c93-70\" data-is-intersecting=\"true\">\r\n<section class=\"text-token-text-primary w-full focus:outline-none has-data-writing-block:pointer-events-none [&amp;:has([data-writing-block])&gt;*]:pointer-events-auto R6Vx5W_threadScrollVars scroll-mb-[calc(var(--scroll-root-safe-area-inset-bottom,0px)+var(--thread-response-height))] scroll-mt-[calc(var(--header-height)+min(200px,max(70px,20svh)))]\" dir=\"auto\" data-turn-id=\"request-6a83414b-92f8-83e9-901e-ae9b28767c93-70\" data-turn-id-container=\"request-6a83414b-92f8-83e9-901e-ae9b28767c93-70\" data-testid=\"conversation-turn-924\" data-turn=\"assistant\">\r\n<div class=\"text-base my-auto mx-auto pb-8 [--thread-content-margin:var(--thread-content-margin-xs,calc(var(--spacing)*4))] @w-sm/main:[--thread-content-margin:var(--thread-content-margin-sm,calc(var(--spacing)*6))] @w-lg/main:[--thread-content-margin:var(--thread-content-margin-lg,calc(var(--spacing)*16))] px-(--thread-content-margin)\">\r\n<div data-conversation-screenshot-content=\"\" class=\"[--thread-content-max-width:40rem] @w-lg/main:[--thread-content-max-width:48rem] mx-auto max-w-(--thread-content-max-width) flex-1 group/turn-messages focus-visible:outline-hidden relative flex w-full min-w-0 flex-col agent-turn\">\r\n<div class=\"flex max-w-full flex-col gap-4 grow\">\r\n<div data-message-author-role=\"assistant\" data-message-id=\"4cb9432a-1a37-4f34-bd89-d378ded27997\" dir=\"auto\" data-message-model-slug=\"gpt-5-6-mini\" class=\"min-h-8 text-message relative flex w-full flex-col items-end gap-2 text-start break-words whitespace-normal outline-none keyboard-focused:focus-ring [.text-message+&amp;]:mt-1\" data-turn-start-message=\"true\" tabindex=\"0\">\r\n<div class=\"flex w-full flex-col gap-1 empty:hidden\">\r\n<div class=\"fbskMG_root yWcLfW_streamingContainer markdown prose dark:prose-invert wrap-break-word w-full dark markdown-new-styling\">\r\n<p data-start=\"65\" data-end=\"198\"><strong data-start=\"84\" data-end=\"112\">Streptococcus pneumoniae</strong><span> </span>is the<span> </span><strong data-start=\"120\" data-end=\"187\">commonest bacterial cause of community-acquired pneumonia (CAP)</strong><span> </span>in adults.</p>\r\n<ul data-start=\"200\" data-end=\"474\">\r\n<li data-start=\"200\" data-end=\"233\">\r\n<p data-start=\"202\" data-end=\"233\"><strong data-start=\"202\" data-end=\"233\">S. pneumoniae → most common</strong></p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"234\" data-end=\"322\">\r\n<p data-start=\"236\" data-end=\"322\"><em data-start=\"236\" data-end=\"259\">Klebsiella pneumoniae</em><span> </span>→ more associated with severe pneumonia in certain risk groups</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"323\" data-end=\"418\">\r\n<p data-start=\"325\" data-end=\"418\"><em data-start=\"325\" data-end=\"348\">Legionella pneumoniae</em><span> </span>is incorrect nomenclature; the organism is<span> </span><strong data-start=\"392\" data-end=\"418\">Legionella pneumophila</strong></p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"419\" data-end=\"474\">\r\n<p data-start=\"421\" data-end=\"474\"><em data-start=\"421\" data-end=\"436\">N. pneumoniae</em><span> </span>is not a standard common CAP pathogen</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p data-start=\"476\" data-end=\"553\" data-is-last-node=\"\" data-is-only-node=\"\"><strong data-start=\"476\" data-end=\"491\">Exam pearl:</strong><br data-start=\"491\" data-end=\"494\"><strong data-start=\"494\" data-end=\"553\" data-is-last-node=\"\">“Commonest organism in CAP = Streptococcus pneumoniae.”</strong></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"z-0 flex min-h-[46px] justify-start\"></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div data-conversation-screenshot-content=\"\" class=\"[--thread-content-max-width:40rem] @w-lg/main:[--thread-content-max-width:48rem] mx-auto max-w-(--thread-content-max-width) flex-1\">\r\n<div></div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</section>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>"}, {"id": "5", "question": "৫) Which is the most common fate of tuberculosis?", "option1": "progressive spread", "option2": "abscess formation", "option3": "effusion formation", "option4": "healing with scar &amp; calcification", "answer": "4", "exp": "<p data-start=\"72\" data-end=\"224\">The<span> </span><strong data-start=\"95\" data-end=\"136\">most common fate of tuberculosis (TB)</strong>, particularly in primary infection, is<span> </span><strong data-start=\"176\" data-end=\"187\">healing</strong><span> </span>with fibrosis and<span> </span><strong data-start=\"206\" data-end=\"223\" data-is-only-node=\"\">calcification</strong>.</p>\r\n<ul data-start=\"226\" data-end=\"430\">\r\n<li data-start=\"226\" data-end=\"266\">\r\n<p data-start=\"228\" data-end=\"266\"><strong data-start=\"228\" data-end=\"266\">Healing → fibrosis + calcification</strong></p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"267\" data-end=\"319\">\r\n<p data-start=\"269\" data-end=\"319\">Progressive spread → occurs in a minority of cases</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"320\" data-end=\"350\">\r\n<p data-start=\"322\" data-end=\"350\">Abscess formation → uncommon</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"351\" data-end=\"430\">\r\n<p data-start=\"353\" data-end=\"430\">Effusion formation → may occur as a complication but is not the usual outcome</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p data-start=\"432\" data-end=\"519\" data-is-last-node=\"\" data-is-only-node=\"\"><strong data-start=\"432\" data-end=\"447\">Exam pearl:</strong><br data-start=\"447\" data-end=\"450\"><strong data-start=\"450\" data-end=\"519\" data-is-last-node=\"\">“Most common fate of TB → Healing by fibrosis and calcification.”</strong></p>"}, {"id": "6", "question": "৬) How many sequences or stages are there in lobar pneumonia?", "option1": "2", "option2": "3", "option3": "4", "option4": "5", "answer": "3", "exp": "<p data-start=\"40\" data-end=\"123\"><strong data-start=\"59\" data-end=\"78\">Lobar pneumonia</strong><span> </span>classically progresses through<span> </span><strong data-start=\"110\" data-end=\"122\">4 stages</strong>:</p>\r\n<ol data-start=\"125\" data-end=\"423\">\r\n<li data-start=\"125\" data-end=\"202\">\r\n<p data-start=\"128\" data-end=\"202\"><strong data-start=\"128\" data-end=\"142\">Congestion</strong><span> </span>– vascular engorgement, edema, and bacterial proliferation.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"203\" data-end=\"277\">\r\n<p data-start=\"206\" data-end=\"277\"><strong data-start=\"206\" data-end=\"226\">Red hepatization</strong><span> </span>– alveoli fill with RBCs, neutrophils, and fibrin.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"278\" data-end=\"356\">\r\n<p data-start=\"281\" data-end=\"356\"><strong data-start=\"281\" data-end=\"302\">Gray hepatization</strong><span> </span>– RBCs break down; fibrin and leukocytes predominate.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"357\" data-end=\"423\">\r\n<p data-start=\"360\" data-end=\"423\"><strong data-start=\"360\" data-end=\"374\">Resolution</strong><span> </span>– exudate is enzymatically digested and cleared.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n<p data-start=\"425\" data-end=\"541\" data-is-last-node=\"\" data-is-only-node=\"\"><strong data-start=\"425\" data-end=\"440\">Exam pearl:</strong><br data-start=\"440\" data-end=\"443\"><strong data-start=\"443\" data-end=\"541\" data-is-last-node=\"\">“Lobar pneumonia = 4 stages → Congestion → Red hepatization → Gray hepatization → Resolution.”</strong></p>"}, {"id": "7", "question": "৭) Secondary tuberculosis can occur by following ways except.....?", "option1": "reactivation", "option2": "regeneration", "option3": "reinfection", "option4": "directly from primary lesion", "answer": "2", "exp": "<p data-start=\"51\" data-end=\"112\"><strong data-start=\"70\" data-end=\"96\">Secondary tuberculosis</strong><span> </span>can develop by:</p>\r\n<ul data-start=\"114\" data-end=\"264\">\r\n<li data-start=\"114\" data-end=\"158\">\r\n<p data-start=\"116\" data-end=\"158\"><strong data-start=\"116\" data-end=\"132\">Reactivation</strong><span> </span>of a latent primary focus</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"159\" data-end=\"210\">\r\n<p data-start=\"161\" data-end=\"210\"><strong data-start=\"161\" data-end=\"176\">Reinfection</strong><span> </span>with<span> </span><em data-start=\"182\" data-end=\"210\">Mycobacterium tuberculosis</em></p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"211\" data-end=\"264\">\r\n<p data-start=\"213\" data-end=\"264\"><strong data-start=\"213\" data-end=\"233\">Direct extension</strong><span> </span>from a previous/primary lesion</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p data-start=\"266\" data-end=\"322\"><strong data-start=\"266\" data-end=\"282\">Regeneration</strong><span> </span>is<span> </span><strong data-start=\"286\" data-end=\"293\">not</strong><span> </span>a mechanism of secondary TB.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"324\" data-end=\"434\" data-is-last-node=\"\" data-is-only-node=\"\" class=\"yWcLfW_streamingTextBlock\"><strong data-start=\"324\" data-end=\"339\">Exam pearl:</strong><br data-start=\"339\" data-end=\"342\"><strong data-start=\"342\" data-end=\"434\" data-is-last-node=\"\">“Secondary TB → Reactivation + Reinfection + Direct spread; Regeneration = not a cause.”</strong></p>"}, {"id": "8", "question": "৮) What is the most common mode of infection in lung abscess?", "option1": "septic embolism", "option2": "parapneumonic", "option3": "lung tumors", "option4": "aspiration of infected materials", "answer": "4", "exp": "<p data-start=\"71\" data-end=\"333\">The<span> </span><strong data-start=\"94\" data-end=\"180\">most common mode of infection in a lung abscess is aspiration of infected material</strong>, particularly from the<span> </span><strong data-start=\"204\" data-end=\"218\">oropharynx</strong>. This is especially associated with impaired consciousness, alcoholism, poor dentition, or swallowing dysfunction.</p>\r\n<ul data-start=\"335\" data-end=\"551\">\r\n<li data-start=\"335\" data-end=\"369\">\r\n<p data-start=\"337\" data-end=\"369\"><strong data-start=\"337\" data-end=\"369\">Aspiration → commonest cause</strong></p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"370\" data-end=\"421\">\r\n<p data-start=\"372\" data-end=\"421\"><strong data-start=\"372\" data-end=\"421\">Parapneumonic spread → may cause lung abscess</strong></p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"422\" data-end=\"457\">\r\n<p data-start=\"424\" data-end=\"457\"><strong data-start=\"424\" data-end=\"457\">Septic embolism → less common</strong></p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"458\" data-end=\"551\">\r\n<p data-start=\"460\" data-end=\"551\"><strong data-start=\"460\" data-end=\"551\">Lung tumors → can cause secondary infection/obstruction but are not the commonest cause</strong></p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p data-start=\"553\" data-end=\"659\" data-is-last-node=\"\" data-is-only-node=\"\" class=\"yWcLfW_streamingTextBlock\"><strong data-start=\"553\" data-end=\"568\">Exam pearl:</strong><br data-start=\"568\" data-end=\"571\"><strong data-start=\"571\" data-end=\"659\" data-is-last-node=\"\">“Lung abscess → most commonly due to aspiration of infected oropharyngeal contents.”</strong></p>"}, {"id": "9", "question": "৯) What is type of most tumors arising from lung?", "option1": "carcinoma", "option2": "sarcoma", "option3": "adenoma", "option4": "fibroma", "answer": "1", "exp": "<p data-start=\"48\" data-end=\"170\">Most<span> </span><strong data-start=\"72\" data-end=\"95\">primary lung tumors</strong><span> </span>are<span> </span><strong data-start=\"100\" data-end=\"114\">carcinomas</strong>, arising from the<span> </span><strong data-start=\"133\" data-end=\"169\" data-is-only-node=\"\">bronchial/respiratory epithelium</strong>.</p>\r\n<ul data-start=\"172\" data-end=\"283\">\r\n<li data-start=\"172\" data-end=\"220\">\r\n<p data-start=\"174\" data-end=\"220\"><strong data-start=\"174\" data-end=\"220\">Carcinoma → most common primary lung tumor</strong></p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"221\" data-end=\"241\">\r\n<p data-start=\"223\" data-end=\"241\"><strong data-start=\"223\" data-end=\"241\">Sarcoma → rare</strong></p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"242\" data-end=\"262\">\r\n<p data-start=\"244\" data-end=\"262\"><strong data-start=\"244\" data-end=\"262\">Adenoma → rare</strong></p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"263\" data-end=\"283\">\r\n<p data-start=\"265\" data-end=\"283\"><strong data-start=\"265\" data-end=\"283\">Fibroma → rare</strong></p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p data-start=\"285\" data-end=\"338\" data-is-last-node=\"\" data-is-only-node=\"\"><strong data-start=\"285\" data-end=\"300\">Exam pearl:</strong><br data-start=\"300\" data-end=\"303\"><strong data-start=\"303\" data-end=\"338\" data-is-last-node=\"\">“Most lung tumors = Carcinoma.”</strong></p>"}, {"id": "10", "question": "১০) Which one can be affected by tuberculosis?", "option1": "myocardium", "option2": "skeletal muscles", "option3": "smooth muscles", "option4": "thyroid", "answer": "4", "exp": "<div class=\"qMYqUG_convSearchResultHighlightRoot\">\r\n<div class=\"\" data-turn-id-container=\"request-6a83414b-92f8-83e9-901e-ae9b28767c93-76\" data-is-intersecting=\"true\">\r\n<section class=\"text-token-text-primary w-full focus:outline-none has-data-writing-block:pointer-events-none [&amp;:has([data-writing-block])&gt;*]:pointer-events-auto R6Vx5W_threadScrollVars scroll-mb-[calc(var(--scroll-root-safe-area-inset-bottom,0px)+var(--thread-response-height))] scroll-mt-[calc(var(--header-height)+min(200px,max(70px,20svh)))]\" dir=\"auto\" data-turn-id=\"request-6a83414b-92f8-83e9-901e-ae9b28767c93-76\" data-turn-id-container=\"request-6a83414b-92f8-83e9-901e-ae9b28767c93-76\" data-testid=\"conversation-turn-936\" data-turn=\"assistant\">\r\n<div class=\"text-base my-auto mx-auto pb-8 [--thread-content-margin:var(--thread-content-margin-xs,calc(var(--spacing)*4))] @w-sm/main:[--thread-content-margin:var(--thread-content-margin-sm,calc(var(--spacing)*6))] @w-lg/main:[--thread-content-margin:var(--thread-content-margin-lg,calc(var(--spacing)*16))] px-(--thread-content-margin)\">\r\n<div data-conversation-screenshot-content=\"\" class=\"[--thread-content-max-width:40rem] @w-lg/main:[--thread-content-max-width:48rem] mx-auto max-w-(--thread-content-max-width) flex-1 group/turn-messages focus-visible:outline-hidden relative flex w-full min-w-0 flex-col agent-turn\">\r\n<div class=\"flex max-w-full flex-col gap-4 grow\">\r\n<div data-message-author-role=\"assistant\" data-message-id=\"c35a38de-5e1a-4c71-8d9c-9302415dfa60\" dir=\"auto\" data-message-model-slug=\"gpt-5-6-mini\" class=\"min-h-8 text-message relative flex w-full flex-col items-end gap-2 text-start break-words whitespace-normal outline-none keyboard-focused:focus-ring [.text-message+&amp;]:mt-1\" data-turn-start-message=\"true\" tabindex=\"0\">\r\n<div class=\"flex w-full flex-col gap-1 empty:hidden\">\r\n<div class=\"fbskMG_root yWcLfW_streamingContainer markdown prose dark:prose-invert wrap-break-word w-full dark markdown-new-styling\">\r\n<p data-start=\"48\" data-end=\"237\" class=\"PDq2pG_selectionAnchorContainer\"><strong data-start=\"67\" data-end=\"119\">Tuberculosis can rarely affect the thyroid gland</strong>, causing<span> </span><strong data-start=\"129\" data-end=\"156\">tuberculous thyroiditis</strong>. Although uncommon, the thyroid can be involved by<span> </span><em data-start=\"208\" data-end=\"236\">Mycobacterium tuberculosis</em>.</p>\r\n<ul data-start=\"239\" data-end=\"398\">\r\n<li data-start=\"239\" data-end=\"283\">\r\n<p data-start=\"241\" data-end=\"283\"><strong data-start=\"241\" data-end=\"283\">Thyroid → can be affected by TB (rare)</strong></p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"284\" data-end=\"312\">\r\n<p data-start=\"286\" data-end=\"312\"><strong data-start=\"286\" data-end=\"312\">Myocardium → very rare</strong></p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"313\" data-end=\"351\">\r\n<p data-start=\"315\" data-end=\"351\"><strong data-start=\"315\" data-end=\"351\">Skeletal muscle → extremely rare</strong></p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"352\" data-end=\"398\">\r\n<p data-start=\"354\" data-end=\"398\"><strong data-start=\"354\" data-end=\"398\">Smooth muscle → not a typical site of TB</strong></p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p data-start=\"400\" data-end=\"484\" data-is-last-node=\"\" data-is-only-node=\"\"><strong data-start=\"400\" data-end=\"415\">Exam pearl:</strong><br data-start=\"415\" data-end=\"418\"><strong data-start=\"418\" data-end=\"484\" data-is-last-node=\"\">“TB can rarely involve the thyroid → tuberculous thyroiditis.”</strong></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"z-0 flex min-h-[46px] justify-start\"></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div data-conversation-screenshot-content=\"\" class=\"[--thread-content-max-width:40rem] @w-lg/main:[--thread-content-max-width:48rem] mx-auto max-w-(--thread-content-max-width) flex-1\">\r\n<div></div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</section>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>"}, {"id": "11", "question": "১১) What is the most common &amp; important aetiological factor in development of lung cancer?", "option1": "smoking tobacco", "option2": "industrial hazards", "option3": "air pollution", "option4": "precursor lesions", "answer": "1", "exp": "<p data-start=\"54\" data-end=\"327\"><strong data-start=\"73\" data-end=\"92\">Tobacco smoking</strong><span> </span>is the<span> </span><strong data-start=\"100\" data-end=\"148\">most important and common etiological factor</strong><span> </span>for the development of<span> </span><strong data-start=\"172\" data-end=\"187\">lung cancer</strong>. It is strongly associated with almost all major histological types, particularly<span> </span><strong data-start=\"270\" data-end=\"297\">squamous cell carcinoma</strong><span> </span>and<span> </span><strong data-start=\"302\" data-end=\"326\">small-cell carcinoma</strong>.</p>\r\n<ul data-start=\"329\" data-end=\"553\">\r\n<li data-start=\"329\" data-end=\"374\">\r\n<p data-start=\"331\" data-end=\"374\"><strong data-start=\"331\" data-end=\"374\">Smoking → major preventable risk factor</strong></p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"375\" data-end=\"419\">\r\n<p data-start=\"377\" data-end=\"419\"><strong data-start=\"377\" data-end=\"419\">Industrial hazards → occupational risk</strong></p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"420\" data-end=\"461\">\r\n<p data-start=\"422\" data-end=\"461\"><strong data-start=\"422\" data-end=\"461\">Air pollution → contributes to risk</strong></p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"462\" data-end=\"553\">\r\n<p data-start=\"464\" data-end=\"553\"><strong data-start=\"464\" data-end=\"553\">Precursor lesions → may precede some cancers but are not the major etiological factor</strong></p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p data-start=\"555\" data-end=\"640\" data-is-last-node=\"\" data-is-only-node=\"\" class=\"yWcLfW_streamingTextBlock\"><strong data-start=\"555\" data-end=\"570\">Exam pearl:</strong><br data-start=\"570\" data-end=\"573\"><strong data-start=\"573\" data-end=\"640\" data-is-last-node=\"\">“Most important risk factor for lung cancer = Tobacco smoking.”</strong></p>"}, {"id": "12", "question": "১২) What is the mode of transmission of PTB?", "option1": "skin contact", "option2": "direct inhalation", "option3": "sexual contact", "option4": "feco-oral", "answer": "2", "exp": "<p data-start=\"56\" data-end=\"364\" class=\"PDq2pG_selectionAnchorContainer\"><strong data-start=\"75\" data-end=\"107\">Pulmonary tuberculosis (PTB)</strong><span> </span>is transmitted mainly through the<span> </span><strong data-start=\"142\" data-end=\"160\">airborne route</strong>. When a person with infectious pulmonary TB<span> </span><strong data-start=\"205\" data-end=\"242\">coughs, sneezes, speaks, or sings</strong>, they release tiny infectious droplet nuclei containing<span> </span><em data-start=\"299\" data-end=\"327\">Mycobacterium tuberculosis</em>, which can be<span> </span><strong data-start=\"342\" data-end=\"353\">inhaled</strong><span> </span>by others.</p>\r\n<ul data-start=\"366\" data-end=\"512\">\r\n<li data-start=\"366\" data-end=\"402\">\r\n<p data-start=\"368\" data-end=\"402\"><strong data-start=\"368\" data-end=\"402\">Direct inhalation → main route</strong></p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"403\" data-end=\"439\">\r\n<p data-start=\"405\" data-end=\"439\">Skin contact → not the usual route</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"440\" data-end=\"478\">\r\n<p data-start=\"442\" data-end=\"478\">Sexual contact → not the usual route</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"479\" data-end=\"512\">\r\n<p data-start=\"481\" data-end=\"512\">Feco-oral → not the usual route</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p data-start=\"514\" data-end=\"608\" data-is-last-node=\"\" data-is-only-node=\"\"><strong data-start=\"514\" data-end=\"529\">Exam pearl:</strong><br data-start=\"529\" data-end=\"532\"><strong data-start=\"532\" data-end=\"608\" data-is-last-node=\"\">“PTB transmission = Airborne → inhalation of infectious droplet nuclei.”</strong></p>"}, {"id": "13", "question": "১৩) Lung cancers arises most often in &amp; around...... of the lung?", "option1": "apex", "option2": "pleura", "option3": "hilus", "option4": "base", "answer": "3", "exp": "<div class=\"qMYqUG_convSearchResultHighlightRoot\">\r\n<div class=\"\" data-turn-id-container=\"request-6a83414b-92f8-83e9-901e-ae9b28767c93-79\" data-is-intersecting=\"true\">\r\n<section class=\"text-token-text-primary w-full focus:outline-none has-data-writing-block:pointer-events-none [&amp;:has([data-writing-block])&gt;*]:pointer-events-auto R6Vx5W_threadScrollVars scroll-mb-[calc(var(--scroll-root-safe-area-inset-bottom,0px)+var(--thread-response-height))] scroll-mt-[calc(var(--header-height)+min(200px,max(70px,20svh)))]\" dir=\"auto\" data-turn-id=\"request-6a83414b-92f8-83e9-901e-ae9b28767c93-79\" data-turn-id-container=\"request-6a83414b-92f8-83e9-901e-ae9b28767c93-79\" data-testid=\"conversation-turn-942\" data-turn=\"assistant\">\r\n<div class=\"text-base my-auto mx-auto pb-8 [--thread-content-margin:var(--thread-content-margin-xs,calc(var(--spacing)*4))] @w-sm/main:[--thread-content-margin:var(--thread-content-margin-sm,calc(var(--spacing)*6))] @w-lg/main:[--thread-content-margin:var(--thread-content-margin-lg,calc(var(--spacing)*16))] px-(--thread-content-margin)\">\r\n<div data-conversation-screenshot-content=\"\" class=\"[--thread-content-max-width:40rem] @w-lg/main:[--thread-content-max-width:48rem] mx-auto max-w-(--thread-content-max-width) flex-1 group/turn-messages focus-visible:outline-hidden min-h-8 relative flex w-full min-w-0 flex-col agent-turn\">\r\n<div class=\"flex max-w-full flex-col gap-4 grow\">\r\n<div data-message-author-role=\"assistant\" data-message-id=\"f07f217c-adfb-4c47-80e7-26c340643641\" dir=\"auto\" data-message-model-slug=\"gpt-5-6-mini\" class=\"min-h-8 text-message relative flex w-full flex-col items-end gap-2 text-start break-words whitespace-normal outline-none keyboard-focused:focus-ring [.text-message+&amp;]:mt-1\" data-turn-start-message=\"true\" tabindex=\"0\">\r\n<div class=\"flex w-full flex-col gap-1 empty:hidden\">\r\n<div class=\"fbskMG_root streaming-animation yWcLfW_streamingContainer markdown prose dark:prose-invert wrap-break-word w-full dark markdown-new-styling\">\r\n<p data-start=\"44\" data-end=\"236\"><strong data-start=\"63\" data-end=\"122\">Lung cancers most commonly arise in or around the hilum</strong>, particularly from the<span> </span><strong data-start=\"146\" data-end=\"170\">bronchial epithelium</strong><span> </span>of the larger bronchi. These are termed<span> </span><strong data-start=\"211\" data-end=\"235\">central/hilar tumors</strong>.</p>\r\n<ul data-start=\"238\" data-end=\"408\">\r\n<li data-start=\"238\" data-end=\"289\">\r\n<p data-start=\"240\" data-end=\"289\"><strong data-start=\"240\" data-end=\"289\">Hilus → common site of central lung carcinoma</strong></p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"290\" data-end=\"336\">\r\n<p data-start=\"292\" data-end=\"336\"><strong data-start=\"292\" data-end=\"336\">Apex → may be involved in Pancoast tumor</strong></p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"337\" data-end=\"372\">\r\n<p data-start=\"339\" data-end=\"372\"><strong data-start=\"339\" data-end=\"372\">Pleura → site of mesothelioma</strong></p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"373\" data-end=\"408\">\r\n<p data-start=\"375\" data-end=\"408\"><strong data-start=\"375\" data-end=\"408\">Base → not the commonest site</strong></p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p data-start=\"410\" data-end=\"474\" data-is-last-node=\"\" data-is-only-node=\"\" class=\"yWcLfW_streamingTextBlock\"><strong data-start=\"410\" data-end=\"425\">Exam pearl:</strong><br data-start=\"425\" data-end=\"428\"><strong data-start=\"428\" data-end=\"474\" data-is-last-node=\"\">“Lung carcinoma → commonly central/hilar.”</strong></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div data-conversation-screenshot-content=\"\" class=\"[--thread-content-max-width:40rem] @w-lg/main:[--thread-content-max-width:48rem] mx-auto max-w-(--thread-content-max-width) flex-1\">\r\n<div></div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</section>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>"}, {"id": "14", "question": "১৪) Which is reservoir of infection of M. bovis?", "option1": "infected cows", "option2": "infected dogs", "option3": "infected birds", "option4": "infected rats", "answer": "1", "exp": "<div class=\"qMYqUG_convSearchResultHighlightRoot\">\r\n<div class=\"\" data-turn-id-container=\"request-6a83414b-92f8-83e9-901e-ae9b28767c93-80\" data-is-intersecting=\"true\">\r\n<section class=\"text-token-text-primary w-full focus:outline-none has-data-writing-block:pointer-events-none [&amp;:has([data-writing-block])&gt;*]:pointer-events-auto R6Vx5W_threadScrollVars scroll-mb-[calc(var(--scroll-root-safe-area-inset-bottom,0px)+var(--thread-response-height))] scroll-mt-[calc(var(--header-height)+min(200px,max(70px,20svh)))]\" dir=\"auto\" data-turn-id=\"request-6a83414b-92f8-83e9-901e-ae9b28767c93-80\" data-turn-id-container=\"request-6a83414b-92f8-83e9-901e-ae9b28767c93-80\" data-testid=\"conversation-turn-944\" data-turn=\"assistant\">\r\n<div class=\"text-base my-auto mx-auto pb-8 [--thread-content-margin:var(--thread-content-margin-xs,calc(var(--spacing)*4))] @w-sm/main:[--thread-content-margin:var(--thread-content-margin-sm,calc(var(--spacing)*6))] @w-lg/main:[--thread-content-margin:var(--thread-content-margin-lg,calc(var(--spacing)*16))] px-(--thread-content-margin)\">\r\n<div data-conversation-screenshot-content=\"\" class=\"[--thread-content-max-width:40rem] @w-lg/main:[--thread-content-max-width:48rem] mx-auto max-w-(--thread-content-max-width) flex-1 group/turn-messages focus-visible:outline-hidden min-h-8 relative flex w-full min-w-0 flex-col agent-turn\">\r\n<div class=\"flex max-w-full flex-col gap-4 grow\">\r\n<div data-message-author-role=\"assistant\" data-message-id=\"d51df97c-a8c6-4fd5-98bd-14a6a5c341cc\" dir=\"auto\" data-message-model-slug=\"gpt-5-6-mini\" class=\"min-h-8 text-message relative flex w-full flex-col items-end gap-2 text-start break-words whitespace-normal outline-none keyboard-focused:focus-ring [.text-message+&amp;]:mt-1\" data-turn-start-message=\"true\" tabindex=\"0\">\r\n<div class=\"flex w-full flex-col gap-1 empty:hidden\">\r\n<div class=\"fbskMG_root streaming-animation yWcLfW_streamingContainer markdown prose dark:prose-invert wrap-break-word w-full dark markdown-new-styling\">\r\n<p data-start=\"52\" data-end=\"214\"><strong data-start=\"71\" data-end=\"94\">Mycobacterium bovis</strong><span> </span>primarily infects<span> </span><strong data-start=\"113\" data-end=\"123\">cattle</strong>, which serve as the main<span> </span><strong data-start=\"149\" data-end=\"175\">reservoir of infection</strong>. Humans can acquire infection through:</p>\r\n<ul data-start=\"216\" data-end=\"323\">\r\n<li data-start=\"216\" data-end=\"270\">\r\n<p data-start=\"218\" data-end=\"270\">Consumption of<span> </span><strong data-start=\"233\" data-end=\"270\">unpasteurized milk/dairy products</strong></p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"271\" data-end=\"323\">\r\n<p data-start=\"273\" data-end=\"323\">Less commonly, direct contact with infected cattle</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p data-start=\"325\" data-end=\"395\" data-is-last-node=\"\" data-is-only-node=\"\" class=\"yWcLfW_streamingTextBlock\"><strong data-start=\"325\" data-end=\"340\">Exam pearl:</strong><br data-start=\"340\" data-end=\"343\"><strong data-start=\"343\" data-end=\"395\" data-is-last-node=\"\">“M. bovis → Reservoir = Cattle (infected cows).”</strong></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div data-conversation-screenshot-content=\"\" class=\"[--thread-content-max-width:40rem] @w-lg/main:[--thread-content-max-width:48rem] mx-auto max-w-(--thread-content-max-width) flex-1\">\r\n<div></div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</section>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>"}, {"id": "15", "question": "১৫) Which type of lung cancers are common in women?", "option1": "squamous cell carcinoma", "option2": "small cell carcinoma", "option3": "adenocarcinoma", "option4": "large cell carcinoma", "answer": "3", "exp": "<p data-start=\"53\" data-end=\"211\"><strong data-start=\"72\" data-end=\"90\">Adenocarcinoma</strong><span> </span>is the<span> </span><strong data-start=\"98\" data-end=\"142\">most common type of lung cancer in women</strong><span> </span>and is also the most common lung cancer overall in many populations.</p>\r\n<ul data-start=\"213\" data-end=\"457\">\r\n<li data-start=\"213\" data-end=\"254\">\r\n<p data-start=\"215\" data-end=\"254\"><strong data-start=\"215\" data-end=\"254\">Adenocarcinoma → commonest in women</strong></p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"255\" data-end=\"346\">\r\n<p data-start=\"257\" data-end=\"346\"><strong data-start=\"257\" data-end=\"346\">Squamous cell carcinoma → historically associated with smoking and more common in men</strong></p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"347\" data-end=\"408\">\r\n<p data-start=\"349\" data-end=\"408\"><strong data-start=\"349\" data-end=\"408\">Small-cell carcinoma → strongly associated with smoking</strong></p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"409\" data-end=\"457\">\r\n<p data-start=\"411\" data-end=\"457\"><strong data-start=\"411\" data-end=\"457\">Large-cell carcinoma → relatively uncommon</strong></p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p data-start=\"459\" data-end=\"521\" data-is-last-node=\"\" data-is-only-node=\"\" class=\"yWcLfW_streamingTextBlock\"><strong data-start=\"459\" data-end=\"474\">Exam pearl:</strong><br data-start=\"474\" data-end=\"477\"><strong data-start=\"477\" data-end=\"521\" data-is-last-node=\"\">“Lung cancer in women → Adenocarcinoma.”</strong></p>"}, {"id": "16", "question": "১৬) What type of hypersensitivity occurs in PTB?", "option1": "Type-1", "option2": "Type-2", "option3": "Type-3", "option4": "Type-4", "answer": "4", "exp": "<p data-start=\"62\" data-end=\"237\" class=\"PDq2pG_selectionAnchorContainer\"><strong data-start=\"81\" data-end=\"113\">Pulmonary tuberculosis (PTB)</strong><span> </span>is associated with<span> </span><strong data-start=\"133\" data-end=\"176\">Type IV (delayed-type) hypersensitivity</strong>, which is<span> </span><strong data-start=\"187\" data-end=\"206\">T-cell mediated</strong><span> </span>rather than antibody-mediated.</p>\r\n<ul data-start=\"239\" data-end=\"507\">\r\n<li data-start=\"239\" data-end=\"288\">\r\n<p data-start=\"241\" data-end=\"288\"><strong data-start=\"241\" data-end=\"266\">Type I → IgE-mediated</strong><span> </span>→ asthma, anaphylaxis</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"289\" data-end=\"362\">\r\n<p data-start=\"291\" data-end=\"362\"><strong data-start=\"291\" data-end=\"332\">Type II → antibody-mediated cytotoxic</strong><span> </span>→ autoimmune hemolytic anemia</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"363\" data-end=\"425\">\r\n<p data-start=\"365\" data-end=\"425\"><strong data-start=\"365\" data-end=\"403\">Type III → immune complex-mediated</strong><span> </span>→ SLE, serum sickness</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"426\" data-end=\"507\">\r\n<p data-start=\"428\" data-end=\"507\"><strong data-start=\"428\" data-end=\"457\">Type IV → T-cell mediated</strong><span> </span>→<span> </span><strong data-start=\"460\" data-end=\"507\">TB, tuberculin reaction, contact dermatitis</strong></p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p data-start=\"509\" data-end=\"589\" data-is-last-node=\"\" data-is-only-node=\"\"><strong data-start=\"509\" data-end=\"524\">Exam pearl:</strong><br data-start=\"524\" data-end=\"527\"><strong data-start=\"527\" data-end=\"589\" data-is-last-node=\"\">“TB → Type IV hypersensitivity → delayed T-cell response.”</strong></p>"}, {"id": "17", "question": "১৭) Which Ig mediates allergic reaction in atopic asthma?", "option1": "IgA", "option2": "IgG", "option3": "IgE", "option4": "IgM", "answer": "3", "exp": "<p data-start=\"42\" data-end=\"164\"><strong data-start=\"61\" data-end=\"78\">Atopic asthma</strong><span> </span>is a<span> </span><strong data-start=\"84\" data-end=\"132\">Type I (immediate) hypersensitivity reaction</strong>, mediated primarily by<span> </span><strong data-start=\"156\" data-end=\"163\">IgE</strong>.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"166\" data-end=\"373\">Allergen exposure →<span> </span><strong data-start=\"186\" data-end=\"204\">IgE production</strong><span> </span>→ IgE binds to<span> </span><strong data-start=\"220\" data-end=\"234\">mast cells</strong><span> </span>→ re-exposure causes mast-cell degranulation → release of histamine and other mediators →<span> </span><strong data-start=\"325\" data-end=\"372\">bronchoconstriction and airway inflammation</strong>.</p>\r\n<ul data-start=\"375\" data-end=\"519\">\r\n<li data-start=\"375\" data-end=\"421\">\r\n<p data-start=\"377\" data-end=\"421\"><strong data-start=\"377\" data-end=\"421\">IgE → allergic reactions / atopic asthma</strong></p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"422\" data-end=\"450\">\r\n<p data-start=\"424\" data-end=\"450\"><strong data-start=\"424\" data-end=\"450\">IgA → mucosal immunity</strong></p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"451\" data-end=\"483\">\r\n<p data-start=\"453\" data-end=\"483\"><strong data-start=\"453\" data-end=\"483\">IgG → major serum antibody</strong></p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"484\" data-end=\"519\">\r\n<p data-start=\"486\" data-end=\"519\"><strong data-start=\"486\" data-end=\"519\">IgM → primary immune response</strong></p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p data-start=\"521\" data-end=\"591\" data-is-last-node=\"\" data-is-only-node=\"\"><strong data-start=\"521\" data-end=\"536\">Exam pearl:</strong><br data-start=\"536\" data-end=\"539\"><strong data-start=\"539\" data-end=\"591\" data-is-last-node=\"\">“Atopic asthma → Type I hypersensitivity → IgE.”</strong></p>"}, {"id": "18", "question": "১৮) Which is uncommon site for tuberculosis?", "option1": "lung", "option2": "skin", "option3": "intestine", "option4": "oropharynx", "answer": "2", "exp": "<p data-start=\"43\" data-end=\"260\">The<span> </span><strong data-start=\"66\" data-end=\"110\">skin is an uncommon site of tuberculosis</strong>. TB primarily affects the<span> </span><strong data-start=\"137\" data-end=\"146\">lungs</strong>, while extrapulmonary involvement can occur in sites such as the<span> </span><strong data-start=\"212\" data-end=\"259\" data-is-only-node=\"\">intestine, lymph nodes, bones, and meninges</strong>.</p>\r\n<ul data-start=\"262\" data-end=\"424\">\r\n<li data-start=\"262\" data-end=\"289\">\r\n<p data-start=\"264\" data-end=\"289\"><strong data-start=\"264\" data-end=\"289\">Lung → commonest site</strong></p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"290\" data-end=\"338\">\r\n<p data-start=\"292\" data-end=\"338\"><strong data-start=\"292\" data-end=\"338\">Intestine → recognized extrapulmonary site</strong></p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"339\" data-end=\"382\">\r\n<p data-start=\"341\" data-end=\"382\"><strong data-start=\"341\" data-end=\"382\">Oropharynx → rare but can be involved</strong></p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"383\" data-end=\"424\">\r\n<p data-start=\"385\" data-end=\"424\"><strong data-start=\"385\" data-end=\"424\">Skin → uncommon site (cutaneous TB)</strong></p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p data-start=\"426\" data-end=\"477\" data-is-last-node=\"\" data-is-only-node=\"\"><strong data-start=\"426\" data-end=\"441\">Exam pearl:</strong><br data-start=\"441\" data-end=\"444\"><strong data-start=\"444\" data-end=\"477\" data-is-last-node=\"\">“Uncommon site of TB → Skin.”</strong></p>"}, {"id": "19", "question": "১৯) What type of emphysema occurs in alpha-1 antitrypsin deficiency?", "option1": "centriacinar", "option2": "panacinar", "option3": "paraseptal", "option4": "irregular", "answer": "2", "exp": "<p data-start=\"58\" data-end=\"212\"><strong data-start=\"77\" data-end=\"111\">Alpha-1 antitrypsin deficiency</strong><span> </span>causes<span> </span><strong data-start=\"119\" data-end=\"155\">panacinar (panlobular) emphysema</strong>, classically affecting the<span> </span><strong data-start=\"183\" data-end=\"198\">lower lobes</strong><span> </span>of the lungs.</p>\r\n<ul data-start=\"214\" data-end=\"411\">\r\n<li data-start=\"214\" data-end=\"257\">\r\n<p data-start=\"216\" data-end=\"257\"><strong data-start=\"216\" data-end=\"257\">Panacinar → α₁-antitrypsin deficiency</strong></p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"258\" data-end=\"308\">\r\n<p data-start=\"260\" data-end=\"308\"><strong data-start=\"260\" data-end=\"308\">Centriacinar → smoking, commonly upper lobes</strong></p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"309\" data-end=\"368\">\r\n<p data-start=\"311\" data-end=\"368\"><strong data-start=\"311\" data-end=\"368\">Paraseptal → associated with spontaneous pneumothorax</strong></p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"369\" data-end=\"411\">\r\n<p data-start=\"371\" data-end=\"411\"><strong data-start=\"371\" data-end=\"411\">Irregular → associated with scarring</strong></p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p data-start=\"413\" data-end=\"489\" data-is-last-node=\"\" data-is-only-node=\"\" class=\"yWcLfW_streamingTextBlock\"><strong data-start=\"413\" data-end=\"428\">Exam pearl:</strong><br data-start=\"428\" data-end=\"431\"><strong data-start=\"431\" data-end=\"489\" data-is-last-node=\"\">“A1AT deficiency → Panacinar emphysema → lower lobes.”</strong></p>"}, {"id": "20", "question": "২০) What type of necrosis is present in Ghon complex?", "option1": "coagulative", "option2": "liquefactive", "option3": "caseous", "option4": "suppurative", "answer": "3", "exp": "<p data-start=\"55\" data-end=\"266\">A<span> </span><strong data-start=\"76\" data-end=\"92\">Ghon complex</strong><span> </span>is the characteristic lesion of<span> </span><strong data-start=\"125\" data-end=\"149\">primary tuberculosis</strong>, consisting of a<span> </span><strong data-start=\"167\" data-end=\"181\">Ghon focus</strong><span> </span>in the lung along with involvement of the draining lymphatics and hilar lymph nodes.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"268\" data-end=\"348\">The necrosis within the tuberculous granuloma is typically<span> </span><strong data-start=\"327\" data-end=\"347\">caseous necrosis</strong>.</p>\r\n<ul data-start=\"350\" data-end=\"549\">\r\n<li data-start=\"350\" data-end=\"387\">\r\n<p data-start=\"352\" data-end=\"387\"><strong data-start=\"352\" data-end=\"387\">Caseous necrosis → Tuberculosis</strong></p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"388\" data-end=\"436\">\r\n<p data-start=\"390\" data-end=\"436\"><strong data-start=\"390\" data-end=\"436\">Coagulative necrosis → ischemia/infarction</strong></p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"437\" data-end=\"492\">\r\n<p data-start=\"439\" data-end=\"492\"><strong data-start=\"439\" data-end=\"492\">Liquefactive necrosis → brain infarction, abscess</strong></p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"493\" data-end=\"549\">\r\n<p data-start=\"495\" data-end=\"549\"><strong data-start=\"495\" data-end=\"549\">Suppurative necrosis → bacterial infection/abscess</strong></p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p data-start=\"551\" data-end=\"624\" data-is-last-node=\"\" data-is-only-node=\"\"><strong data-start=\"551\" data-end=\"566\">Exam pearl:</strong><br data-start=\"566\" data-end=\"569\"><strong data-start=\"569\" data-end=\"624\" data-is-last-node=\"\">“TB → Caseous necrosis; Primary TB → Ghon complex.”</strong></p>"}]}, "_source": "archive-question-subject", "_exam_id": 307, "custom_field": "", "exam_time": "420000", "is_omr": false, "omr_time": "7200000", "examname": "Jun 21, 2018", "type": "BCS-Health-Long", "payment": "BALANCE_NOT"}